From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: dram: h616: give the MAHB MBUS port priority

The EMAC is an AHB master and reaches DRAM through MBUS port 2 (MAHB).
With TX in store-and-forward mode (Linux, MTU above 4 KiB) it starts a
frame larger than its 4 KiB TX FIFO once the FIFO is full and must then
read the rest from DRAM at line rate. Under CPU and video decoder load
the TX FIFO runs empty: in MAC loopback at 1 Gbit/s 6% of 8192-byte,
20% of 9014-byte and about 70% of 13000-16376-byte frames underflowed.
With the port 2 priority bit set: 0 of 4000 frames (60-16376 bytes),
the same load before and after.

Set the priority bit of port 2, as already done for port 25. It applies
to every master behind MAHB, not only the EMAC.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
@@ -71,7 +71,8 @@
 
 	MBUS_CONF(0, false, HIGHEST, 0,  256,  128,  100);
 	MBUS_CONF(1, false,    HIGH, 0, 1536, 1400,  256);
-	MBUS_CONF(2, false, HIGHEST, 0,  512,  256,   96);
+	/* MAHB: the EMAC TX FIFO underflows under load without priority */
+	MBUS_CONF(2,  true, HIGHEST, 0,  512,  256,   96);
 	MBUS_CONF(3, false,    HIGH, 0,  256,  100,   80);
 	MBUS_CONF(4, false,    HIGH, 2, 8192, 5500, 5000);
 	MBUS_CONF(5, false,    HIGH, 2,  100,   64,   32);
